Assignment 4. React Profile Card using Props 
• Aim: To build a reusable Profile Card component in React and pass dynamic data 
using Props. 
• Learning Objectives: Set up a React project using Vite or Create React App, 
understand JSX, functional components, and unidirectional data flow (Props). 
• Theoretical Background: Props (properties) are read-only configuration objects 
passed from parent components to child components to render dynamic data. 
• Detailed Requirements: 
o Create a parent component (e.g., App) containing a list of user profiles 
(objects with name, imageUrl, and description). 
o Create a child functional component named ProfileCard. 
o Pass data from the parent to the child component via props. 
o Render the card with clean UI layout (using inline styles or CSS modules). 

